.\logs\codex-20261028T0056040098517Z-0e3e812f999949619f3ef537642fd6e6.log:2635:.\logs\codex-20261028T0050330184002Z-083ce22b36a74990a69855563700d944.log:2818:logs\codex-20261028T0044337148261Z-e67ee9f4ea9c4e89a0db4aaf7b10f2d7.log:523:.\docs\WORKFLOW.md:251:The minimal issuer reads a UTF-8 JSON specification with exactly four keys: `request`, `artifact_approval`, `prerequisite_approval`, and `expires_utc`. `request` has exactly `action` (`verify` or `upgrade`), `environment`, `expected_start`, `target`, `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Both approval references have exactly `id` (canonical UUID) and `sha256` (SHA-256 of the approval file's exact bytes). `expires_utc` must be UTC, later than issuance, and no more than 24 hours later. Manifest/framework/revision hashes retain the existing `sha256-utf8-lf` normalization; approval-file and predecessor-claim hashes use exact bytes.
